  "step": [
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1,
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Planning your backsplash tile project properly can save you a lot of headaches and ensure you get a stunning result. First things first, measure your wall carefully and then plan your tile layout. You'll want to figure out how the tiles will fit around outlets, cabinets, and countertops so you avoid awkward tiny cuts at the edges. Next, think about your substrate prep; the wall needs to be clean, dry, and flat for the tiles to adhere well. Then, consider the type of tile you're using. Will it need sealing, or does it require a specific type of grout? These details matter! Don't forget about how the edges will be terminated – will you use a schluter trim, caulk, or just a clean cut edge? Making these decisions upfront ensures a smoother installation. A detailed plan helps avoid surprises and ensures your backsplash looks fantastic. If you're feeling unsure about any of these steps, HH Remodeling LLC is always here to help guide you through the process and achieve that perfect look."
    }
  ],
